1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,480
~Nankatsu - Shizuoka~

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,980
Hey, Kumi, what's wrong?

3
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:13,650
You were going to tell him after the national cup, right?

4
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:18,620
Yes, but Tsubasa-senpai went to Europe after that.

5
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:21,910
The tournament is over, but he still only thinks about football.

6
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:24,120
It can't be helped.

7
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,790
That's what makes Tsubasa-kun attractive anyway.

8
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,170
Senpai.

9
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,670
Right, Sanae?

10
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,050
Nakazawa-senpai.

11
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:35,800
Kumi-chan.

12
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:41,430
I wish you both the best, I'm not taking sides.

13
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:50,190
Yukari-senpai, when will Tsubasa-senpai return to Japan?

14
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:55,200
After the International Youth Tournament in France.

15
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,490
Then, I guess next term.

16
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:00,410
What? That long?

17
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:06,040
Yes, there's no such thing as summer vacation for Tsubasa-kun and the others.

18
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,000
They're all chasing football.

19
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:19,220
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

20
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:42,510
~France~

21
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:49,770
Episode 7

22
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:49,770
In this tournament we have 3 wins and 2 losses.

23
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:54,020
We arrived in France with a good result, coach.

24
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,780
Yes, thanks to you, Misugi-kun.

25
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,650
Especially in the last three matches.

26
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:05,700
The formation and your decision to put Matsuyama in defensive support were good.

27
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:13,210
Coach, that worked because Tsubasa-kun controlled the midfield.

28
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,790
With Tsubasa-kun at the center,

29
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:21,050
the line of Hyuga, Matsuyama, and Wakashimazu became much more solid.

30
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:24,180
As usual, you have keen observations about the team.

31
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,100
What?

32
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:27,810
Even though you're sitting on the bench,

33
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:31,810
I noticed that you're playing on the field in your head.

34
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:33,190
Coach.

35
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:36,150
I have to say this for the International Youth Tournament,

36
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:38,820
I registered you as a player.

37
00:03:39,070 --> 00:03:40,320
What?

38
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,820
Katagiri-san, where is Misaki?

39
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,870
He's not showing up at the airport.

40
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:52,670
I gave him the Japan jersey and asked him to join.

41
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:54,790
But he seemed undecided.

42
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:55,710
What?

43
00:03:56,290 --> 00:03:58,920
It's been three years since he played with you.

44
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,300
Apparently, his worry was whether he could still fit in with you

45
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:05,890
after this three-year break.

46
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,350
Misaki-kun.

47
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:12,100
I'm Taro Misaki.

48
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:17,060
It's fine, Misaki-kun will overcome it.

49
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:23,950
When you just arrived, there was no problem with your combination play.

50
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:26,950
I believe in you, Misaki-kun.

51
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:32,540
I believe you'll join the Japan youth team and we can do our combination play again.

52
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,330
Alright guys, the tournament is in 3 days.

53
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:39,920
~Japan team's accommodation~

54
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:41,880
That's all for today, get plenty of rest.

55
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:42,970
Yes, coach.

56
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,930
Tsubasa.

57
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:58,480
The coach told us to rest today, but I still can't sit still.

58
00:05:06,490 --> 00:05:08,320
So this is Paris.

59
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:15,960
And that's the Eiffel Tower. Alright, I've made my decision.

60
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:22,170
I remember the day I arrived in Nankatsu.

61
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:26,300
I couldn't sit still and went into town to practice dribbling.

62
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:34,980
That's where I met Ishizaki-kun, Wakabayashi-kun, and Roberto.

63
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:34,980
Nankatsu

64
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:37,560
Oh, the Eiffel Tower!

65
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:40,310
Wow, it's so tall.

66
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:57,210
What!? Mi-Misaki-kun!?

67
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:00,920
Tsubasa-kun.

68
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:02,420
Misaki-kun.

69
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,630
Long time no see, Misaki-kun.

70
00:06:04,710 --> 00:06:07,630
Tsubasa-kun, it really is you!

71
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:12,300
Ozora Tsubasa and Taro Misaki, Nankatsu's Golden Duo.

72
00:06:12,390 --> 00:06:17,940
Or rather, the Japan Team's Golden Duo, finally reunited after 3 years.

73
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:20,980
But you haven't changed at all, Tsubasa-kun.

74
00:06:21,770 --> 00:06:25,190
The ball is still your friend.

75
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:29,200
You're the same.

76
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,950
By the way, Misaki-kun, about joining the Japan team...

77
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:35,660
I'll do it.

78
00:06:35,910 --> 00:06:38,460
Let's do our combination play like in the old days.

79
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:41,080
O-Okay, Misaki-kun.

80
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:47,300
Hooray! Hooray! The Japan team is finally at its best.

81
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:53,800
Jujo, I think you deserve a beating.

82
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:55,140
Get ready.

83
00:06:57,310 --> 00:07:00,060
You're the ones who will get beaten.

84
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:05,820
Strong.

85
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,070
It's too late for this.

86
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,570
Finish him off.

87
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:12,450
Who are you?

88
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,700
I said finish, get out of here.

89
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:22,830
What's your problem?

90
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:28,590
It was 5 against 1 and you're not even congratulating me?

91
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,050
You're from Nankatsu Middle School.

92
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:33,970
Your family has a boxing gym.

93
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:39,890
Kanda, Koshi Kanda. Are you from Nankatsu Middle School too?

94
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:44,980
Boxers shouldn't use their skills for fighting.

95
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:47,730
I don't applaud someone who doesn't follow the rules.

96
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,110
He's bleeding.

97
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:59,830
Also, some people can create wonders without throwing a single punch.

98
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:20,520
Special news: Japan's successful performance in the world

99
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:18,310
Look, look, did you see?

100
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:20,350
Hey, Yukari.

101
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,020
The French National Tournament begins! Middle schoolers using all their strength! Japan won on the world stage.

102
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:28,480
No doubt, that's Ozora Tsubasa.

103
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,020
Ozora Tsubasa

104
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,820
Sanae.

105
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:36,030
~Japan's training ground in France~

106
00:08:38,030 --> 00:08:40,290
I'm Taro Misaki, pleased to meet you.

107
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:41,500
Misaki!

108
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,710
Misaki, it's been a long time.

109
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,710
How are you, Misaki?

110
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:51,210
The tournament is in 2 days, let's train.

111
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,300
Yes, coach!

112
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:56,550
Pair up, I want you to do forward passes and shoot.

113
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,930
Goalkeeper, guard the goal.

114
00:08:59,260 --> 00:09:00,140
Yes, coach.

115
00:09:01,890 --> 00:09:04,310
Alright, Tsubasa and Misaki you're the first pair.

116
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:06,230
- O-Okay. - O-Okay.

117
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,150
Tsubasa and Misaki.

118
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:14,150
It's been 3 years since their last combination play.

119
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:17,320
So can they still coordinate?

120
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,160
Misaki-kun.

121
00:09:25,210 --> 00:09:26,370
Tsubasa-kun.

122
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:31,590
- Alright, ready, Misaki-kun? - Yes!

123
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:32,840
Catch.

124
00:09:33,010 --> 00:09:33,960
Okay.

125
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,970
Oh, this...

126
00:09:40,350 --> 00:09:41,470
Tsubasa-kun.

127
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:42,970
Misaki-kun.

128
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:48,440
3 years have passed, but they're playing in perfect harmony.

129
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,070
Their speed and accuracy never diminish.

130
00:09:51,150 --> 00:09:54,440
Of course, why do you think they're called the Golden Duo?

131
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:57,860
- Amazing. - The Golden Duo is back.

132
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,570
The final pass, Misaki-kun.

133
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:01,950
Okay.

134
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:09,710
Your shot was great, Misaki-kun.

135
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:11,420
Your pass was great, Tsubasa-kun.

136
00:10:11,670 --> 00:10:14,000
Bravo, both of you were great.

137
00:10:14,090 --> 00:10:16,420
Those passes, those shots, that speed...

138
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:19,430
Misaki has improved a lot here in France.

139
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,260
That's what I'd expect from you, Tsubasa-kun.

140
00:10:21,350 --> 00:10:24,010
3 years have passed and you still surprise me.

141
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:27,180
I could barely keep up with your feet.

142
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:32,690
So do you, now we just have to do this in the match.

143
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:33,690
Yes.

144
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:36,820
Alright guys, don't let Tsubasa and Misaki get past you.

145
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:38,700
I want to see your sweat.

146
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:39,990
Yes, coach!

147
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:41,950
- Get ready. - Okay.

148
00:10:42,030 --> 00:10:42,950
Catch.

149
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:46,950
Great, Wakashimazu.

150
00:10:47,410 --> 00:10:49,250
Your reflexes are weak, Wakashimazu.

151
00:10:49,330 --> 00:10:52,710
Why are you punching the ball instead of catching it with both hands?

152
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:53,710
What!?

153
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,090
Wakabayashi.

154
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,590
What are you doing!?

155
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,720
Your passes are not coordinated at all.

156
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,340
How did you get selected for this team?

157
00:11:02,550 --> 00:11:03,970
What?

158
00:11:04,050 --> 00:11:05,100
Wakabayashi-san.

159
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,100
Wakabayashi-kun.

160
00:11:07,430 --> 00:11:09,350
Your overlaps are too slow.

161
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,310
What are you doing!?

162
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,860
You'll lose like this.

163
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:17,230
This shot won't work against the best in the world.

164
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:18,740
Wakabayashi!

165
00:11:19,610 --> 00:11:20,450
Hyuga!

166
00:11:20,530 --> 00:11:21,490
Hyuga-san!

167
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:26,040
Alright, that's enough for today, go rest.

168
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,240
O-Okay.

169
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:35,590
Tsubasa-kun.

170
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:40,380
He's changed a lot now.

171
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:42,970
Since the Hamburg match, Wakabayashi

172
00:11:43,050 --> 00:11:45,390
hasn't stopped putting us down.

173
00:11:45,470 --> 00:11:48,270
Yes, as if he's trying to pick a fight.

174
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,060
I know, he's a member of a big European club.

175
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:54,560
He gained high skills in Europe.

176
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:59,030
But we're working hard too, and he criticizes our every move.

177
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,490
For the International Youth Tournament,

178
00:12:01,570 --> 00:12:04,450
Maybe Wakabayashi could be the goalkeeper.

179
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,530
What?

180
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:11,910
Perhaps, Coach Mikami was previously Wakabayashi's personal trainer.

181
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,630
Wakabayashi-kun.

182
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,840
Is it you, Tsubasa?

183
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,680
The day after tomorrow is an important day.

184
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:25,800
Yes.

185
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:29,680
Do your best, Tsubasa, for Japan.

186
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:33,640
I'm not thinking of playing this time.

187
00:12:33,730 --> 00:12:34,560
What?

188
00:12:34,810 --> 00:12:38,940
If I join the team, your teamwork will be disrupted.

189
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:40,440
Wakabayashi-kun.

190
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:44,740
They definitely made progress in this tournament.

191
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:47,910
They focused their anger and fighting spirit on me and worked harder.

192
00:12:47,990 --> 00:12:49,870
That made all of them improve.

193
00:12:49,950 --> 00:12:53,080
It was worth criticizing them so much.

194
00:12:53,830 --> 00:12:55,080
Th-Then...

195
00:12:55,710 --> 00:13:00,340
This strengthened the Japan team, I'm glad I played the villain.

196
00:13:01,090 --> 00:13:03,880
Everyone started thinking about their playing style.

197
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:09,010
And Wakashimazu now has more motivation,

198
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,180
to become the main goalkeeper of the Japan team.

199
00:13:12,850 --> 00:13:15,850
This time I'm giving him that opportunity.

200
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:18,230
Wakabayashi-kun, you...

201
00:13:19,110 --> 00:13:22,570
But despite all the progress, the level of national competition

202
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:26,610
is much higher than you think, Tsubasa.

203
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:28,120
Y-Yeah.

204
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:33,160
And the one who will unite this Japan team, Tsubasa, is you.

205
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:34,120
I'm counting on you.

206
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,710
Wakabayashi-kun.

207
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:38,170
Okay, Wakabayashi-kun.

208
00:13:40,710 --> 00:13:42,960
Wa-Wakabayashi.

209
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:48,010
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

210
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,950
Born: June 21, Height: 168 cm, Weight: 57 kg, Blood Type: B

211
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:52,410
~France~

212
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:57,160
The first International Youth Tournament starts tomorrow in France.

213
00:13:57,450 --> 00:14:00,710
Along with hosts France, the German youth,

214
00:14:00,790 --> 00:14:03,670
strong contenders for the championship, have now checked in.

215
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:06,590
Oh, there it is, Schneider at the front.

216
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:10,180
~Germany Youth~

217
00:14:06,670 --> 00:14:09,260
- Schester, the playmaker. - That's Kaltz, the strategy master.

218
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:12,680
He's the top candidate for top scorer in this championship.

219
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,720
The number one player in Europe,

220
00:14:14,810 --> 00:14:18,230
Karl Heinz Schneider, we can't wait to see his game.

221
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:21,100
Hey, the Italian team is here too.

222
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:24,020
~Italy Youth~

223
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,980
You're right, hurry up.

224
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:28,240
The Italians have the great goalkeeper Gino Hernandez.

225
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,280
Yes.

226
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:31,450
Gino Hernandez.

227
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:33,950
Wakabayashi from Hamburg or him,

228
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:36,120
this tournament will determine the best.

229
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:38,000
Watch out.

230
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,790
Hey, that pass is weak.

231
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,210
Hello, so you're working hard?

232
00:14:43,170 --> 00:14:46,050
Coach Diaz, Pascal.

233
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:49,590
Thanks for scouting the European teams, Coach Valoise.

234
00:14:49,670 --> 00:14:52,050
How are the other teams?

235
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:54,300
How was it, Diaz?

236
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:58,390
There were a few players worth watching.

237
00:14:58,850 --> 00:15:00,930
Nothing to be afraid of.

238
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:07,070
Listen up kids, let's show those Europeans how South America plays football.

239
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:11,530
We can beat everyone with our talent.

240
00:15:11,610 --> 00:15:12,450
Diaz!

241
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:15,530
No doubt Argentina will be champions!

242
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:16,950
Yes!

243
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:22,250
Coach Carabonara has sharp eyes.

244
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:25,960
I'll be playing with you too, nice to meet you.

245
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:29,300
This is Louis Napoleon, please give him a warm welcome.

246
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:32,470
So that's Louis Napoleon.

247
00:15:37,350 --> 00:15:41,890
I've heard some not-so-good rumors about him.

248
00:15:43,190 --> 00:15:48,020
He has talent, but he's always been expelled for bad behavior.

249
00:15:48,150 --> 00:15:50,320
He's also been suspended.

250
00:15:51,030 --> 00:15:53,650
The notorious Louis Napoleon.

251
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:57,120
Coach, you brought a time bomb right before the tournament.

252
00:15:57,200 --> 00:16:00,200
Does he really want to win?

253
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:03,620
You're the playmaker, aren't you?

254
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:06,920
Just pass to me.

255
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:10,920
If you do that, France will definitely win.

256
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,930
Hey, I got important news.

257
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:20,260
Misaki is playing for Japan in this tournament.

258
00:16:20,350 --> 00:16:21,930
What? Are you sure?

259
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:27,020
Now we have to support both Japan and France.

260
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:27,940
Yes!

261
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:31,280
Tomorrow is an important tournament, let's focus.

262
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,190
Yes, coach.

263
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:36,280
Right, our first opponent is the Italians.

264
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:39,370
They refused the match, thinking it wasn't worth playing us.

265
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:42,200
They'll regret that.

266
00:16:42,450 --> 00:16:43,330
Catch.

267
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:46,670
Run guys, go faster.

268
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,540
Speed up the transition between offense and defense.

269
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,090
- Okay. - Okay, Tsubasa.

270
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:52,710
- Nitta, hit it to the right. - Okay.

271
00:16:55,010 --> 00:16:55,970
Tsubasa.

272
00:16:56,220 --> 00:16:57,590
Nice, Hyuga-kun.

273
00:16:57,890 --> 00:16:59,220
Okay.

274
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:03,140
Your shot was great, Hyuga.

275
00:17:03,470 --> 00:17:05,430
Yes, good timing.

276
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,730
They're improving their movements.

277
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:08,940
Damn it.

278
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:11,070
Next time I'll definitely catch it.

279
00:17:11,150 --> 00:17:12,610
That's the spirit, Wakashimazu.

280
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:13,820
Wakabayashi.

281
00:17:16,490 --> 00:17:19,200
I'll win, I'll beat Wakabayashi with my skill.

282
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:22,030
The main goalkeeper position is mine.

283
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,700
Great catch, Wakashimazu.

284
00:17:25,290 --> 00:17:27,040
Alright, let's go, Misaki.

285
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,040
Okay.

286
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:35,670
In just 2 days they paired up and are completely in sync.

287
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:36,590
Yes.

288
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:41,100
No matter how strong their combination play is, it works against any opponent.

289
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:45,810
Tsubasa and Misaki earned the name Golden Duo.

290
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:47,980
Coach, we need to talk.

291
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,980
Matsuyama.

292
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:55,860
Hey, what is the defense doing? Work harder.

293
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:59,200
What are you saying, Wakabayashi? Stop mocking...

294
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:00,610
Enough, Soda.

295
00:18:01,030 --> 00:18:02,490
Hyuga, you think so too.

296
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:05,120
There's no point in arguing.

297
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:09,500
Save this for our Italy match tomorrow.

298
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:11,040
Alright.

299
00:18:12,380 --> 00:18:13,750
Hyuga.

300
00:18:14,210 --> 00:18:15,460
Hyuga-kun.

301
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:20,010
Alright, we're continuing training, let's go guys.

302
00:18:20,090 --> 00:18:21,470
Okay.

303
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:25,140
Let's do our best for tomorrow's match.

304
00:18:25,930 --> 00:18:28,390
Right, coach?

305
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:31,900
Tsubasa united the team and gave them spirit.

306
00:18:32,310 --> 00:18:36,150
If anyone deserves to be captain, it's Tsubasa, not me.

307
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,150
Matsuyama.

308
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:43,700
Only Tsubasa can be the captain of the Japan team.

309
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:54,290
Listen to the roar of the crowd, the stadium is completely full.

310
00:18:54,590 --> 00:18:57,960
Now the 12 participating countries are here.

311
00:18:58,050 --> 00:19:00,300
The people of Paris have been waiting for this tournament.

312
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:01,800
It's finally happening.

313
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:05,180
The first International Youth Tournament has begun in France.

314
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:09,930
In the preliminary round, they play in groups of 3 teams.

315
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:13,440
Only 1 team from each group advances to the finals.

316
00:19:13,850 --> 00:19:16,190
Now I draw your attention first

317
00:19:16,270 --> 00:19:20,240
to the German team led by Emperor Karl Heinz Schneider.

318
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:23,200
Germany is the favorite of this tournament.

319
00:19:23,490 --> 00:19:26,700
Germany will definitely win.

320
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:32,620
Besides Schneider, Schester, Kaltz, and Margas are really strong.

321
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,580
Italy youth, playing Japan today.

322
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:39,550
Also one of the strong contenders in the tournament.

323
00:19:40,010 --> 00:19:44,340
Rumor has it Gino Hernandez is Europe's number one goalkeeper.

324
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:46,180
In the qualifiers for this tournament

325
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:48,970
he played 5 matches and didn't concede a single goal.

326
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,730
Argentina from South America should not be underestimated.

327
00:19:52,810 --> 00:19:55,980
Their weapon is individual talent that empowers them.

328
00:19:56,360 --> 00:20:03,280
Rumor has it Argentina's captain Juan Diaz is a once-in-a-century phenomenon.

329
00:20:04,150 --> 00:20:08,120
And the huge crowd is supporting the French youth.

330
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:13,710
Led by famous Coach Carabonara and known as the artist on the field,

331
00:20:13,790 --> 00:20:16,250
Captain El Sid Pierre plays in midfield.

332
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:18,340
France will definitely be champions!

333
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:20,340
Show them the power of European football.

334
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,420
We will.

335
00:20:21,510 --> 00:20:24,880
Our reputation is at stake, so we must win.

336
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:28,470
And last but not least, Japan youth.

337
00:20:28,550 --> 00:20:30,510
You might see some familiar faces.

338
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,930
The Japan team consists of

339
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:37,900
the outstanding players from the recent Middle School Tournament.

340
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:39,860
And there's an interesting development.

341
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:43,280
Wakabayashi-kun, who played brilliantly in Germany,

342
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:47,360
and Misaki-kun, who's been very active in France, are both on the team.

343
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,030
Good luck, Misaki!

344
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,540
Oh, that's Fischer.

345
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:55,460
Misaki, do your best for Japan.

346
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:57,420
Good luck, Misaki!

347
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,090
~Nankatsu - Shizuoka~

348
00:21:03,170 --> 00:21:04,670
Japan is finally entering the field.

349
00:21:03,170 --> 00:21:04,670
Live from France.

350
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:06,220
Tsubasa!

351
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:07,840
We're watching you.

352
00:21:08,470 --> 00:21:09,680
Guys.

353
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,310
We believe in you.

354
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:16,310
Tsubasa-senpai, come home soon.

355
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:19,650
No, I mean, go for the championship with all your strength!

356
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:29,320
Live from France. And finally Japan is entering the field!

357
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:35,330
Live from France. And finally Japan is entering the field!

358
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:38,560
Good luck, Tsubasa-kun!

359
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:41,440
Live from France - The match begins

360
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:48,450
It has finally begun, the International Youth Tournament.

361
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,890
Our first step on the world stage.

362
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:55,790
Our dream of winning the world cup might finally come true.

363
00:21:55,790 --> 00:21:59,600
It's time to stand up and show the world

364
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,610
what we can do.

365
00:23:45,340 --> 00:25:21,170
Next episode: I Am Taro Misaki